AUDIO: 'Nice. I know I had a hard time focusing in there, um but you definitely saw just'

[07:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the end of the wire and that bright light at the end of it. Like I think we found a winner, guys. I\'m going to start bringing these in. It\'s one thing to dodge a shady salesman on the floor, but we\'re trying to dodge'

[07:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'irrelevance here. So, what I was thinking was, "Okay, the robots are cool, but you still need a person to sit there and tell them where to weld." Not exactly automation. I literally stood there and watched the machine scan a part, create a 3D model, and then decide'

[07:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'where it needed to be welded based on that model. That\'s where I really started to wake up because there\'s textile factories in India right now that are putting GoPro cameras on the heads of all of their workers in order'

[07:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to collect training data on the AI. And the same thing is going to happen in the welding industry. The scary part is it doesn\'t even need to happen in America. Any country anywhere that\'s doing welding processes can put these GoPros on and start collecting and training an'

[08:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AI data model that\'s going to be able to scan these parts, create a 3D image of it. The robot will be able to decide where it\'s supposed to weld and how it\'s supposed to weld. If you guys still think hand welding is safe from'

[08:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'automation, you\'ve got to see this next part. Oh, this one has laser scanning with computer vision. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Let\'s see this thing run here. How many directions? Two or three? Usually?'

[08:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; up to you, but normally you will you will require two directions. &gt;&gt; Okay. Here\'s the model generated after the scanning.'

[08:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; So, this also has the same technology with the laser and the photo eye here. So, the laser just increases the contrast so that the camera can read it easier &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; and you know, different light'

[09:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conditions. Also, it\'s doing a scan right now. Here we go. Dual axis positioner robotic welding workstation. You guys can pause and read that if you want. Oh, here it is running its G code down here.'

[09:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There\'s a whole line of inspection cameras right on the gantry. So, pretty much anything you can fit underneath this, it can scan quickly. And then there\'s another one right here on the welding head also.'

[09:29] [scene:talk]
